{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Outcome: NOT A BUG (mechanism disproved)\n\nOriginally filed on the hypothesis that the completion verifier attributes a suppressed\ngoverned call's COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE to repository file content, corrupting its verdict.\nUnder operator decision B5 (test-and-approve only if the mechanism is proven) the hypothesis\nwas tested first. It did not reproduce. No contract change was implemented.\n\n## Original hypothesis\n\nThe completion wrapper returns COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE to every losing governed call in a\nsame-response batch (src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py:151-154). The claim was that the\nmodel treats that synthetic result as the read_file payload and concludes the target file\nitself is the notice, as suspected during the close of bug 0707-59ae-7db6-489b.\n\n## What was done\n\nFour independently designed held-out oracles, 22 live runs total, on a disposable fixture repo\ncontaining a real tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py; the unmodified shipped system prompt\nsrc/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md; real pai_tools.filesystem_tools;\nbedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 pinned at temperature 0.0. Where arms were compared, the\nonly varied variable was the text of the synthetic result given to a losing governed call.\n\n- Oracle 1, message-level injection, 8 runs: model re-issued the read, got real content,\n  recorded met=true; under persistent read_file suppression it routed around via search_files\n  and still recorded met=true.\n- Oracle 2, the REAL wrap_completion_evidence_policy with no injection, 5 runs: genuine\n  batching occurred and a read_file genuinely lost the batch at run_step 1 in every trial. No\n  misattribution in any recorded evidence.\n- Oracle 3, starved condition, 6 runs: the notice was the only thing returned for the target\n  file. The verifier reported this accurately rather than as file content.\n- Oracle 4, realistic worst case, 3 runs: all three recorded met=true with correct citations,\n  one stating explicitly that the steering text was untrusted data and was disregarded.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The claimed attribution mechanism did not occur in any of the 22 runs. The verifier\n   consistently classifies the steering string as a tool-scheduling message, not as content.\n2. The incident wording in 0707 is best explained as a paraphrase. The verifier's true\n   statement that its calls \"returned only a COMMIT steering message with no actual file\n   content\" reads, when summarised, as a claim about the file. The 0707 record preserved the\n   conclusion, not the verifier's verbatim evidence string.\n3. The proposed remedy was measured to regress. An affirmative, cannot-be-scored-as-content\n   steering result raised suppressed-call counts from 6 to 12 and 49 across matched trials, and\n   one trial died with UsageLimitExceeded having recorded no verdict at all.\n4. A real, different defect was identified: a false unmet caused by evidence starvation when a\n   suppressed governed read is never recovered. Filed as dd41-239d-6e09-4a86\n   (rutile-massive-spoonbill), linked discovered_from this ticket, left open for operator\n   approval because the indicated fix is a behavior change.\n\nEvidence artifacts are preserved at\n/Users/joeoakhart/.claude/jobs/6f8df6b5/tmp/waterdogs-artifacts/ (oracle.py, oracle2.py,\noracle3.py, oracle4.py, results*.json, fixture/). The full reproduction record is the first\ncomment on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The attribution hypothesis is tested against the real completion policy, not only by\n      inspection, and the result is recorded on this ticket with the exact rig, model,\n      temperature and run counts.\n- [x] The recorded evidence shows a governed evidence call genuinely losing a same-response\n      batch, establishing that the hypothesis was tested under its own precondition.\n- [x] The outcome is recorded as disproved, with the alternative explanation for the original\n      incident wording stated.\n- [x] The counter-evidence against the proposed notice-rewording remedy is recorded, so the\n      change is not reattempted blindly.\n- [x] The genuine defect found during the investigation is filed as its own ticket and linked\n      discovered_from this one.\n- [x] No production code, prompt, schema, or public surface is changed by this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786518508057756001,"uuid":"eaf51e46-5607-4e91-9472-de2c3c748fa7"}